From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 20:58:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: msm8998: vote for XO from gcc and gpucc in
 the active set only

Every clock that clk-smd-rpm exposes votes in both the RPM active set
and the RPM sleep set when prepared.  gcc's "xo" input is prepared
permanently (gpll0 and the CLK_IS_CRITICAL HMSS branches root on it),
so the APSS sleep set carries a permanent "XO on" vote and RPM can
never enter XO shutdown, no matter what the rest of the system does.

Clocks generated by gcc and gpucc can only be consumed while the
application processor subsystem is running: whenever the sleep set is
actually in effect (RPM-assisted power collapse), nothing clocked by
them can be running.  Components that genuinely need the crystal across
APSS sleep hold it through their own RPM master votes (remoteprocs) or
through dedicated RPM resources with their own enable votes: the PMIC
clock buffers (ln_bb/rf_clk, optionally pin-controlled), the mmcc "xo"
input and the DSI/HDMI PHY refs, all of which keep using the shared
RPM_SMD_XO_CLK_SRC vote.

This mirrors the downstream arrangement, where the permanently-held
CPU-subsystem clocks (gpll0_ao, the HMSS RCG) and the GCC keepalive
vote sit on the active-only cxo_clk_src_ao twin, and the gpucc "xo"
input is explicitly cxo_clk_src_ao ("xo_ao" in the downstream 8998 DT).

The active-set behaviour is unchanged: RPM_SMD_XO_A_CLK_SRC posts the
same enable vote in the active set and is CLK_IS_CRITICAL in
clk-smd-rpm, so the XO reference cannot be dropped while the APSS runs.
Only the sleep-set vote is released.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi
index 29a40e1fe035..7486cdd2d17a 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi
@@ -1376,7 +1376,7 @@ gcc: clock-controller@100000 {
 			reg = <0x00100000 0xb0000>;
 
 			clock-names = "xo", "sleep_clk";
-			clocks = <&rpmcc RPM_SMD_XO_CLK_SRC>, <&sleep_clk>;
+			clocks = <&rpmcc RPM_SMD_XO_A_CLK_SRC>, <&sleep_clk>;
 
 			/*
 			 * The hypervisor typically configures the memory region where these clocks
@@ -2483,7 +2483,7 @@ gpucc: clock-controller@5065000 {
 			#power-domain-cells = <1>;
 			reg = <0x05065000 0x9000>;
 
-			clocks = <&rpmcc RPM_SMD_XO_CLK_SRC>,
+			clocks = <&rpmcc RPM_SMD_XO_A_CLK_SRC>,
 				 <&gcc GCC_GPU_GPLL0_CLK>;
 			clock-names = "xo",
 				      "gpll0";
